# Reading the results
# - "probe sockets still ESTABLISHED" is sampled after the probe process exits, so it is 0 in both runs; the
#   meaningful F1 numbers are node_closed_at and the node's CPU time.
# - F1 before: the node handled all 16,299 replayed-header messages over 20 s after banning the peer and never
#   closed the connection (node CPU +5.7 s). After: the node closed the connection 3.5 ms into the flood, once
#   the ban landed (13 messages were written, most still in socket buffers), and its CPU time did not move.
# - F2 before: behind a withholder the victim connected its first block at +87 s and finished 3,000 blocks at
#   +111 s (honest-only baseline 40 s). After: first block at +9 s, all 3,000 at +38 s (baseline 30 s); one
#   stall rotation logged (2,048 requests moved off the withholder, strike 1).
